The `tools` config lets you enable a whitelist of actions per toolkit (or disable a blacklist). See the **Enabling or disabling specific tools** section of the session‑configuration guide: [/docs/configuring-sessions#enabling-or-disabling-specific-tools](/docs/configuring-sessions#enabling-or-disabling-specific-tools).

Use the **`tools`** configuration to whitelist only the GitHub actions you need. Pass an object keyed by the toolkit slug (`github`) and give an `enable` array with the tool identifiers you want exposed.  

```python
session = composio.sessions.create(
    user_id="user_123",
    toolkits=["github"],                     # load the GitHub toolkit
    tools={                                  # limit to selected tools
        "github": {
            "enable": [
                "GITHUB_CREATE_ISSUE",
                "GITHUB_SEARCH_REPOSITORIES",
            ]
        }
    },
)
```

```typescript
const session = await composio.create("user_123", {
  toolkits: ["github"],
  tools: {
    github: {
      enable: ["GITHUB_CREATE_ISSUE", "GITHUB_SEARCH_REPOSITORIES"],
    },
  },
});
```

Only `GITHUB_CREATE_ISSUE` and `GITHUB_SEARCH_REPOSITORIES` will be available to the agent; all other GitHub tools are hidden. See the **“Enabling or disabling specific tools”** section of the session‑configuration guide for details: [Configuring Sessions – Enabling or disabling specific tools](/docs/configuring-sessions#enabling-or-disabling-specific-tools).

