Use the **“Using sessions via MCP”** guide — the page that walks you through exposing a single user’s session via an MCP endpoint [/docs/sessions-via-mcp](/docs/sessions-via-mcp).  

When you create the session, pass `mcp: true` (or `{ mcp: true }` in TypeScript) so the SDK returns `session.mcp.url` and `session.mcp.headers`. If you want the MCP URL to expose only a fixed set of tools, combine `mcp: true` with the **direct‑tools preset** (`SESSION_PRESET_DIRECT_TOOLS` / `SessionPreset.DIRECT_TOOLS`) and list the toolkits/tools you need. All other session configuration (toolkit filters, auth configs, connected accounts) is done the same way as in the **Configuring Sessions** docs [/docs/configuring-sessions](/docs/configuring-sessions).  

```python
# Python SDK
from composio import Composio, SESSION_PRESET_DIRECT_TOOLS

composio = Composio()
session = composio.sessions.create(
    user_id="user_123",
    toolkits=["gmail"],
    tools={"gmail": {"enable": ["GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS", "GMAIL_CREATE_EMAIL_DRAFT"]}},
    session_preset=SESSION_PRESET_DIRECT_TOOLS,
    mcp=True,
)

mcp_url = session.mcp.url
mcp_headers = session.mcp.headers
```

```typescript
// TypeScript SDK
import { Composio, SessionPreset } from "@composio/core";

const composio = new Composio();
const session = await composio.create("user_123", {
